   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = - x + 2 y \\) with \\( f(1) = 1 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(2) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 1 \\) with three steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         65,
         27
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{2 - (1)}{3} = \\frac{1}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (1, 1) \\) the slope is \\( 1 \\), so \\( y \\approx 1 + (\\frac{1}{3})(1) = \\frac{4}{3} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{4}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            4,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{4}{3}) \\) the slope is \\( \\frac{4}{3} \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{4}{3} + (\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{4}{3}) = \\frac{16}{9} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{5}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            16,
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{5}{3}, \\frac{16}{9}) \\) the slope is \\( \\frac{17}{9} \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{16}{9} + (\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{17}{9}) = \\frac{65}{27} \\) at \\( x = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            65,
            27
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "So \\( f(2) \\approx \\frac{65}{27} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            65,
            27
         ]
      }
   ],
